## Project Architecture

- **Product**: ZerotierB
- **Shape**: Android application (`com.brukb.zerotier`) — one process, two exclusive ZeroTier stacks
- **Platforms**: Android 8.0+ (API 26), `compileSdk` / `targetSdk` 35
- **Primary language**: Kotlin 2.2, JVM 17
- **Build / verify**: `make verify` → `./gradlew :app:lintDebug :app:testDebugUnitTest :core:testDebugUnitTest :app:assembleDebug`

```
ZerotierBApplication
  ConnectionOrchestrator (mutex, RuntimePlan)
    ├── ProxyModeService   (libzt + HttpProxyServer 127.0.0.1)
    └── ZerotierBVpnService (JNI Node + TUN)
AppPreferences.globalMode: OFF | PROXY | VPN | AUTO
LinkProfile (Wi-Fi SSID / per-SIM / Other): OFF | PROXY | VPN
ZerotierBNetwork: enabled + pin-main + createdAt + routePriority — no PROXY/VPN chip
```

**Spec of record for dual-mode:** [`docs/PROXY-VPN-PLAN.md`](../../docs/PROXY-VPN-PLAN.md).
**Delivery sequence:** [`planning/phases/INDEX.md`](../../planning/phases/INDEX.md).

Today the tree is VPN-only (JNI). Dual-mode lands through INDEX tasks. Do not run libzt `Node` and JNI `Node` at the same time. Share `filesDir` identity. HTTP proxy binds **127.0.0.1 only**.

### Inspiration sources

- In-tree JNI client: `app/src/main/java/com/brukb/zerotier/vpn/`
- Archived libzt proxy: git branch `archive/proxy-mode` (`com.zerotier.pylon`)
- Spec: `docs/PROXY-VPN-PLAN.md`

### Build & Run

```bash
make verify          # lint + unit tests + assembleDebug
make install-hooks   # lefthook pre-commit → make verify
./gradlew :app:installDebug
```

